## Detailed Design

### 1. SigLIP Sigmoid Loss (`models/losses.py`)

Replace the symmetric InfoNCE cross-entropy with per-pair binary sigmoid loss:
```
L = -1/n² Σᵢ Σⱼ [ yᵢⱼ log σ(zᵢ·zⱼ · t - b) + (1-yᵢⱼ) log σ(-(zᵢ·zⱼ · t - b)) ]
```
where `yᵢⱼ = 1` for matching pairs, `0` otherwise, and `t`/`b` are learnable temperature/bias.

Also implement **soft-target** variant: build `yᵢⱼ` from text-embedding cosine similarity (not hard 0/1), so near-duplicate reports get soft positive labels instead of being pushed apart.

### 2. Structured Label Auxiliary Heads (`data/structured_labels.py` + model changes)

Parse reports into multi-label attributes using rule-based extraction (with optional LLM enhancement):
- `slowing` (yes/no)
- `epileptiform_discharges` (yes/no)  
- `focal_left` / `focal_right` / `generalized` (lateralization)
- `background_rhythm` (normal/abnormal)
- `frequency_band` mentions (delta/theta/alpha/beta)

Add multi-label classification heads on the EEG embedding, trained jointly with contrastive loss:
```
L_total = L_contrastive + λ_aux * Σₖ L_bce(head_k(eeg_z), label_k)
```

### 3. Channel-Aware Encoder (`models/channel_aware_encoder.py`)

- Tokenize EEG per-channel: each channel becomes a token sequence
- Add **electrode position embeddings** (learnable, indexed by channel identity in the 10-20 system)
- Use **Transformer encoder** layers for cross-channel attention
- **Window-level attention pooling**: when multiple windows come from the same recording, pool them with learned attention weights for recording-level representation

### 4. Learned Prompt Embeddings (`models/prompt_learner.py`)

CoOp-style: instead of fixed text prompts like "This is a normal recording", learn `M` continuous prompt tokens that are prepended to the class-name token embedding:
```
prompt = [v₁][v₂]...[vₘ][CLASS]
```
where `vᵢ` are learnable and `[CLASS]` is the text embedding of the class name.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The original model is preserved — `EEGCLIPPlusPlus` extends `EEGCLIP`, and all new features are gated by config flags so you can ablate any component.

